# Changelog updates

When a change is release-relevant, update the root [`CHANGELOG.md`](../../CHANGELOG.md)
in the same change. Add a concise bullet under the existing `unreleased`
section. Match the current style: one user-facing sentence per bullet, no
version bump, and no new heading.

Do not edit vendored submodule changelogs such as
`spice-protocol/CHANGELOG.md`.

## Update when

- User-visible features or behavior changes
- Bug fixes that affect shipped binaries or the installer
- Compatibility, upgrade, or security fixes
- Other changes that belong in release notes

## Skip when

- Documentation-only edits (`README.md`, comments, assets used only in docs)
- Tests-only or internal refactors with no shipped behavior change
- CI, packaging-script, or deploy/release automation that does not change
  the product users install
- Agent instructions and Cursor rules (including this file)

If a change mixes release-relevant and exempt work, still add a changelog
entry for the release-relevant part.
